ource and has a massive, active community.\\\\n*   **Maturity:** A battle-tested and highly reliable database system.\\\\n\\\\n**Cons:**\\\\n*   **Schema Rigidity:** Requires a well-defined schema upfront. Changes to the schema (migrations) can be more complex than in a NoSQL database, though modern ORMs mitigate this.\\\\n*   **Vertical Scaling:** Traditionally scales vertically (by increasing the resources of a single server), which can be more expensive than the horizontal scaling of some NoSQL databases. For the scale of an HOA, this is not a significant concern.\\\\n\\\\n**Alternative Considered: MongoDB (NoSQL)**\\\\n\\\\n*   **Pros:** Flexible schema is good for rapid prototyping. Scales horizontally easily.\\\\n*   **Cons:** Weaker transactional guarantees by default compared to PostgreSQL. The data for an HOA is naturally structured and relational, making the schema flexibility of NoSQL less of an advantage and more of a potential liability for data consistency.\\\\n\\\\n**Conclusion:** PostgreSQL's emphasis on data integrity and its suitability for relational data make it the superior choice for this project.\\\\n\\\\n### 6. Summary of Recommendations\\\\n\\\\n*   **Architecture:** Modular Service-Oriented Architecture.\\\\n*   **Backend Framework:** **Node.js with TypeScript** (using a framework like Express or NestJS).\\\\n*   **Authentication:** **Auth0 or AWS Cognito** to manage user identities and issue JWTs.\\\\n*   **Data Separation:** **API Middleware** for route protection and a **Database-level RBAC** model.\\\\n*   **Database:** **PostgreSQL** for its reliability and strong data integrity.\\\\n\\\\nThis technology stack represents a modern, secure, and maintainable foundation for the HOA website project. It leverages industry best practices and will serve the needs of the community effectively.\\\\n\\\\nRespectfully Submitted,\\\\n\\\\n**Agent Motti**\\\\nLead Architect\\\\n`8ef59f79-b0eb-4178-9f92-316b4701e61e`\\\"\\n}\\n###MOTTI-REPORT-GIDEON-01###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###ORDER-GIDEON-ORDER-MOTTI-02###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Agent Gideon (cb013e58-2d3a-4cad-adeb-07b249a5c0b9)\\nTo: 8ef59f79-b0eb-4178-9f92-316b4701e61e\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Supervisor Motti, your previous analysis task is now obsolete. New Directive: The project architecture has been decided as Strapi (backend) and Next.js (frontend). Your new task is to conduct a deep-dive analysis and produce a detailed technical specification for the backend. Your report must include: 1. A complete set of API endpoint definitions for Strapi, detailing all routes (e.g., GET /articles, POST /login), expected request bodies, and response payloads. 2. A detailed database schema for PostgreSQL, outlining all tables, columns, data types, and relationships required to support all planned features. This specification is critical for the final DEP. Submit your report upon completion.\\\",\\n  \\\"orderID\\\": \\\"GIDEON-ORDER-MOTTI-02\\\"\\n}\\n###ORDER-GIDEON-ORDER-MOTTI-02###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###ORDER-GIDEON-ORDER-MOTTI-02###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Agent Gideon (cb013e58-2d3a-4cad-adeb-07b249a5c0b9)\\nTo: 8ef59f79-b0eb-4178-9f92-316b4701e61e\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Supervisor Motti (Lead Architect), your original analysis task is now superseded. Our direction has been set. The approved technical foundation for the HOA project is a Next.js frontend with a Strapi backend/CMS. Your new task is to produce a detailed backend technical specification. This must include: 1. A complete set of database schemas (for PostgreSQL) for all data models (Users, Documents, News, etc.). 2. A comprehensive definition of all API endpoints Strapi will expose, including routes, HTTP methods, and expected request/response data structures. Collaborate with Supervisor Tagge to ensure your schema and API definitions align with his CMS configuration plan. Deliver your findings as a formal specification document.\\\",\\n  \\\"orderID\\\": \\\"GIDEON-ORDER-MOTTI-02\\\"\\n}\\n###ORDER-GIDEON-ORDER-MOTTI-02###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###ORDER-GIDEON-ORDER-MOTTI-02###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Agent Gideon (cb013e58-2d3a-4cad-adeb-07b249a5c0b9)\\nTo: 8ef59f79-b0eb-4178-9f92-316b4701e61e\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Supervisor Motti (Lead Architect), your previous order is rescinded. The project's foundational architecture has been approved: a Strapi backend with a PostgreSQL database. Your new task is to produce a detailed backend technical specification. This must include: 1. Complete database schemas for all required content types (Users, News, Documents, etc.). 2. A comprehensive list of API endpoints with defined routes, expected request payloads, and response structures. 3. The role-based access control rules for each endpoint. This specification is critical for the final DEP. Submit your report upon completion.\\\",\\n  \\\"orderID\\\": \\\"GIDEON-ORDER-MOTTI-02\\\"\\n}\\n###ORDER-GIDEON-ORDER-MOTTI-02###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###MOTTI-REPORT-GIDEON-02###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Agent Motti (8ef59f79-b0eb-4178-9f92-316b4701e61e)\\nTo: Agent Gideon (cb013e58-2d3a-4cad-adeb-07b249a5c0b9)\\nType: Report\\nIn-Reply-To: GIDEON-ORDER-MOTTI-02\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"report\\\": \\\"###REPORT###\\\\n**To:** Agent Gideon (cb013e58-2d3a-4cad-adeb-07b249a5c0b9), System Supervisor\\\\n**From:** Agent Motti (8ef59f79-b0eb-4178-9f92-316b4701e61e), Lead Architect\\\\n**Date:** 2023-10-27\\\\n**Subject:** Detailed Backend Technical Specification for HOA Website Project (Strapi)\\\\n**Reference ID:** GIDEON-ORDER-MOTTI-02\\\\n\\\\n***\\\\n\\\\n### 1. Introduction\\\\n\\\\nThis document provides the detailed backend technical specification for the HOA Website Project, in accordance with the directive to use Strapi as the backend content management system and PostgreSQL as the database. This specification outlines the complete database schema and the corresponding API endpoint definitions that will be auto-generated or customized within Strapi.\\\\n\\\\nThe features supported by this specification include user management (Residents, Board Members), announcements, document management with access control, and architectural review submissions.\\\\n\\\\n### 2. Detailed Database Schema (PostgreSQL)\\\\n\\\\nStrapi automatically generates the schema based on defined Content Types. The following tables represent the planned schema. Strapi manages primary keys (`id`), and `created_at`/`updated_at` timestamps automatically.\\\\n\\\\n**Table: `users-permissions_user` (Extended from Strapi Default)**\\\\n\\\\n| Column Name | Data Type | Constraints/Notes |\\\\n|---|---|---|\\\\n| `id` | INTEGER | Primary Key, Auto-incrementing |\\\\n| `username` | VARCHAR(255) | NOT NULL, UNIQUE |\\\\n| `email` | VARCHAR(255) | NOT NULL, UNIQUE |\\\\n| `provider` | VARCHAR(255) | e.g., 'local' for standard auth |\\\\n| `password` | VARCHAR(255) | Hashed password |\\\\n| `resetPasswordToken`| VARCHAR(255) | NULLABLE |\\\\n| `confirmationToken`| VARCHAR(255) | NULLABLE |\\\\n| `confirmed` | BOOLEAN | NOT NULL, DEFAULT FALSE |\\\\n| `blocked` | BOOLEAN | NOT NULL, DEFAULT FALSE |\\\\n| `property_address` | TEXT | **Custom Field:** Resident's address |\\\\n| `phone_number` | VARCHAR(255) | **Custom Field:** Resident's contact number |\\\\n\\\\n*   **Relationship:** Many-to-one with `users-permissions_role`.\\\\n\\\\n**Table: `users-permissions_role` (Strapi Default)**\\\\n\\\\n| Column Name | Data Type | Constraints/Notes |\\\\n|---|---|---|\\\\n| `id` | INTEGER | Primary Key, Auto-incrementing |\\\\n| `name` | VARCHAR(255) | NOT NULL, UNIQUE. Values: `Public`, `Authenticated` (Resident), `BoardMember` |\\\\n| `description` | VARCHAR(255) | |\\\\n| `type` | VARCHAR(255) | e.g., `authenticated` |\\\\n\\\\n**Table: `announcements`**\\\\n\\\\n| Column Name | Data Type | Constraints/Notes |\\\\n|---|---|---|\\\\n| `id` | INTEGER | Primary Key |\\\\n| `title` | VARCHAR(255) | NOT NULL |\\\\n| `content` | TEXT | NOT NULL |\\\\n| `published_at` | TIMESTAMPTZ | Strapi's mechanism for draft/published status |\\\\n\\\\n*   **Relationship:** Many-to-one with `users-permissions_user` (as `created_by`).\\\\n\\\\n**Table: `documents`**\\\\n\\\\n| Column Name | Data Type | Constraints/Notes |\\\\n|---|---|---|\\\\n| `id` | INTEGER | Primary Key |\\\\n| `title` | VARCHAR(255) | NOT NULL |\\\\n| `description` | TEXT | NULLABLE |\\\\n| `access_level` | ENUM | NOT NULL. Values: `public`, `resident`, `board` |\\\\n\\\\n*   **Relationship:** One-to-one with `upload_file` (the actual file). Many-to-one with `document_categories`.\\\\n\\\\n**Table: `document_categories`**\\\\n\\\\n| Column Name | Data Type | Constraints/Notes |\\\\n|---|---|---|\\\\n| `id` | INTEGER | Primary Key |\\\\n| `name` | VARCHAR(255) | NOT NULL, UNIQUE. e.g., 'Meeting Minutes', 'Bylaws' |\\\\n\\\\n**Table: `architectural_reviews`**\\\\n\\\\n| Column Name | Data Type | Constraints/Notes |\\\\n|---|---|---|\\\\n| `id` | INTEGER | Primary Key |\\\\n| `project_title` | VARCHAR(255) | NOT NULL |\\\\n| `project_description`| TEXT | NOT NULL |\\\\n| `status` | ENUM | NOT NULL. Values: `submitted`, `in_review`, `approved`, `denied`, `needs_info` |\\\\n\\\\n*   **Relationships:**\\\\n    *   Many-to-one with `users-permissions_user` (as `submitted_by`).\\\\n    *   One-to-many with `upload_file` (for attachments like plans/photos).\\\\n    *   One-to-many with `architectural_review_comments`.\\\\n\\\\n**Table: `architectural_review_comments`**\\\\n\\\\n| Column Name | Data Type | Constraints/Notes |\\\\n|---|---|---|\\\\n| `id` | INTEGER | Primary Key |\\\\n| `content` | TEXT | NOT NULL |\\\\n\\\\n*   **Relationships:**\\\\n    *   Many-to-one with `users-permissions_user` (as `author`).\\\\n    *   Many-to-one with `architectural_reviews`.\\\\n\\\\n### 3. API Endpoint Definitions\\\\n\\\\nStrapi's `users-permissions` plugin will be configured with three roles: `Public` (unauthenticated), `Authenticated` (standard resident), and `BoardMember` (elevated privileges). Access control is specified for each endpoint.\\\\n\\\\n#### 3.1 Authentication Endpoints (`/api/auth`)\\\\n\\\\n*   **`POST /api/auth/local/register`**\\\\n    *   **Description:** Register a new resident user. Defaults to `Authenticated` role.\\\\n    *   **Authentication:** `Public`\\\\n    *   **Request Body:**\\\\n        ```json\\\\n        {\\\\n          \\\\\\\"username\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"newresident\\\\\\\",\\\\n          \\\\\\\"email\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"new@resident.com\\\\\\\",\\\\n          \\\\\\\"password\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SecurePassword123\\\\\\\",\\\\n          \\\\\\\"property_address\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"123 Maple St\\\\\\\"\\\\n        }\\\\n        ```\\\\n    *   **Success Response (200 OK):**\\\\n        ```json\\\\n        {\\\\n          \\\\\\\"jwt\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"...\\\\\\\",\\\\n          \\\\\\\"user\\\\\\\": { \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": 5, \\\\\\\"username\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"newresident\\\\\\\", ... }\\\\n        }\\\\n        ```\\\\n\\\\n*   **`POST /api/auth/local`**\\\\n    *   **Description:** Log in a user to obtain a JWT.\\\\n    *   **Authentication:** `Public`\\\\n    *   **Request Body:**\\\\n        ```json\\\\n        {\\\\n          \\\\\\\"identifier\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"resident1\\\\\\\", // or email@domain.com\\\\n          \\\\\\\"password\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"ValidPassword123\\\\\\\"\\\\n        }\\\\n        ```\\\\n    *   **Success Response (200 OK):** (Same as register)\\\\n\\\\n#### 3.2 User Endpoints (`/api/users`)\\\\n\\\\n*   **`GET /api/users/me`**\\\\n    *   **Description:** Get the profile of the currently logged-in user.\\\\n    *   **Authentication:** `Authenticated`, `BoardMember`\\\\n    *   **Success Response (200 OK):**\\\\n        ```json\\\\n        {\\\\n          \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": 1,\\\\n          \\\\\\\"username\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"resident1\\\\\\\",\\\\n          \\\\\\\"email\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"resident1@hoa.com\\\\\\\",\\\\n          \\\\\\\"property_address\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"456 Oak Ave\\\\\\\"\\\\n        }\\\\n        ```\\\\n\\\\n#### 3.3 Announcements Endpoints (`/api/announcements`)\\\\n\\\\n*   **`GET /api/announcements`**\\\\n    *   **Description:** Get a list of all published announcements.\\\\n    *   **Authentication:** `Public`\\\\n    *   **Success Response (200 OK):**\\\\n        ```json\\\\n        { \\\\\\\"data\\\\\\\": [ { \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": 1, \\\\\\\"attributes\\\\\\\": { \\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Pool Opening\\\\\\\", ... } } ] }\\\\n        ```\\\\n\\\\n*   **`POST /api/announcements`**\\\\n    *   **Description:** Create a new announcement.\\\\n    *   **Authentication:** `BoardMember`\\\\n    *   **Request Body:**\\\\n        ```json\\\\n        { \\\\\\\"data\\\\\\\": { \\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"New Announcement\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"content\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"...\\\\\\\" } }\\\\n        ```\\\\n    *   **Success Response (200 OK):** Returns the created announcement object.\\\\n\\\\n*   *Other routes (`GET /:id`, `PUT /:id`, `DELETE /:id`) follow standard REST patterns and are restricted to `BoardMember` role.* \\\\n\\\\n#### 3.4 Documents Endpoints (`/api/documents`)\\\\n\\\\n*   **`GET /api/documents`**\\\\n    *   **Description:** Get a list of documents. **This will require a custom controller** to filter results based on the user's role and the document's `access_level` attribute.\\\\n    *   **Authentication:** `Public` (returns only public docs), `Authenticated` (returns public + resident docs), `BoardMember` (returns all docs).\\\\n    *   **Success Response (200 OK):**\\\\n        ```json\\\\n        { \\\\\\\"data\\\\\\\": [ { \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": 1, \\\\\\\"attributes\\\\\\\": { \\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Community Bylaws\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"access_level\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"public\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": { ... } } } ] }\\\\n        ```\\\\n\\\\n*   **`POST /api/documents`**\\\\n    *   **Description:** Upload a new document.\\\\n    *   **Authentication:** `BoardMember`\\\\n    *   **Request Body:** Requires `multipart/form-data` to handle file upload.\\\\n    *   **Success Response (200 OK):** Returns the created document object.\\\\n\\\\n#### 3.5 Architectural Review Endpoints (`/api/architectural-reviews`)\\\\n\\\\n*   **`GET /api/architectural-reviews`**\\\\n    *   **Description:** List architectural reviews. **Custom controller required.** Residents can only see their own submissions. Board Members can see all submissions.\\\\n    *   **Authentication:** `Authenticated`, `BoardMember`\\\\n    *   **Success Response (200 OK):**\\\\n        ```json\\\\n        { \\\\\\\"data\\\\\\\": [ { \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": 1, \\\\\\\"attributes\\\\\\\": { \\\\\\\"project_title\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"New Fence\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"submitted\\\\\\\", ... } } ] }\\\\n        ```\\\\n\\\\n*   **`POST /api/architectural-reviews`**\\\\n    *   **Description:** Submit a new architectural review request.\\\\n    *   **Authentication:** `Authenticated`\\\\n    *   **Request Body:**\\\\n        ```json\\\\n        { \\\\\\\"data\\\\\\\": { \\\\\\\"project_title\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"New Deck\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"project_description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"...\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"submitted\\\\\\\" } }\\\\n        ```\\\\n    *   **Success Response (200 OK):** Returns the created review object.\\\\n\\\\n*   **`POST /api/architectural-reviews/:id/comments`**\\\\n    *   **Description:** Add a comment to a review. \\\\n    *   **Authentication:** `BoardMember` or `Authenticated` (if they are the owner of the review).\\\\n    *   **Request Body:**\\\\n        ```json\\\\n        { \\\\\\\"data\\\\\\\": { \\\\\\\"content\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Please provide material samples.\\\\\\\" } }\\\\n        ```\\\\n    *   **Success Response (200 OK):** Returns the parent review object with the new comment populated.\\\\n\\\\nThis specification provides a comprehensive blueprint for the backend development. Custom logic for role-based filtering will be implemented in Strapi's policies or by overriding the default controllers as noted.\\\\n\\\\nRespectfully Submitted,\\\\n\\\\n**Agent Motti**\\\\nLead Architect\\\\n`8ef59f79-b0eb-4178-9f92-316b4701e61e`\\\"\\n}\\n###MOTTI-REPORT-GIDEON-02###\"}]}],\"config\":{},\"tools\":[],\"output\":{}}}","genkit:state":"success"},"displayName":"generate","links":[],"instrumentationLibrary":{"name":"genkit-tracer","version":"v1"},"spanKind":"INTERNAL","sameProcessAsParentSpan":{"value":true},"status":{"code":0},"timeEvents":{"timeEvent":[]}}},"displayName":"generate","startTime":1751232703398,"endTime":1751232716476.638}